      "article_key": "https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/industry/indl-goods/svs/metals-mining/hindustan-zinc-to-invest-up-to-600-million-this-fiscal-80-capex-earmarked-for-ongoing-projects/articleshow/132636632.cms",
      "canonical_link": "https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/industry/indl-goods/svs/metals-mining/hindustan-zinc-to-invest-up-to-600-million-this-fiscal-80-capex-earmarked-for-ongoing-projects/articleshow/132636632.cms",
      "link": "https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/industry/indl-goods/svs/metals-mining/hindustan-zinc-to-invest-up-to-600-million-this-fiscal-80-capex-earmarked-for-ongoing-projects/articleshow/132636632.cms",
      "title": "Hindustan Zinc to invest up to $600 million this fiscal, 80% capex earmarked for ongoing projects",
      "summary": "KT Corp 관련 기사다. 기사 제목은 'Hindustan Zinc to invest up to $600 million this fiscal, 80% capex earmarked for ongoing projects'이다. Hindustan Zinc plans a significant investment of $500-600 million this fiscal year. Eighty percent of this capital expenditure will fund ongoing projects already in progress. The remaining twenty percent will support new initiatives which the company will announce soon. Approved projects account for 250,000 tonnes of capacity, requiring substantial financial backing. Further expansion to 650 KT will necessitate similar investment over the next four to five years. Further expansion to 650 KT will necessitate similar investment over the next four to five years Reuters Hindustan Zinc plans a significant investment of $500-600 million this fiscal year Vedanta Group company Hindustan Zinc Ltd (HZL) plans to invest $500-600 million (around Rs 5,000 crore) during the current financial year, with the bulk of the capital expenditure directed towards projects already under execution, Chief Executive Officer Arun Misra said However, orders for milling and concentrate-related facilities are yet to be finalised Also Read: Hindustan Zinc plans Rs 50k-crore capex pipeline for next 5 years The remaining expansion, which will take capacity to 650 KT, will require investment in a similar proportion over the next four to five years \"That translates to an average annual capex of about Rs 7,000-8,000 crore,\" Misra said, adding that only 15-20% of this multi-year investment plan will translate into actual cash outflows during the current financial year.",
      "original_title": "Hindustan Zinc to invest up to $600 million this fiscal, 80% capex earmarked for ongoing projects",
      "original_summary": "Hindustan Zinc plans a significant investment of $500-600 million this fiscal year. Eighty percent of this capital expenditure will fund ongoing projects already in progress. The remaining twenty percent will support new initiatives which the company will announce soon. Approved projects account for 250,000 tonnes of capacity, requiring substantial financial backing. Further expansion to 650 KT will necessitate similar investment over the next four to five years.",
      "company_summary": "KT Corp 관련 기사다. 기사 제목은 'Hindustan Zinc to invest up to $600 million this fiscal, 80% capex earmarked for ongoing projects'이다. Hindustan Zinc plans a significant investment of $500-600 million this fiscal year. Eighty percent of this capital expenditure will fund ongoing projects already in progress. The remaining twenty percent will support new initiatives which the company will announce soon. Approved projects account for 250,000 tonnes of capacity, requiring substantial financial backing. Further expansion to 650 KT will necessitate similar investment over the next four to five years. Further expansion to 650 KT will necessitate similar investment over the next four to five years Reuters Hindustan Zinc plans a significant investment of $500-600 million this fiscal year Vedanta Group company Hindustan Zinc Ltd (HZL) plans to invest $500-600 million (around Rs 5,000 crore) during the current financial year, with the bulk of the capital expenditure directed towards projects already under execution, Chief Executive Officer Arun Misra said However, orders for milling and concentrate-related facilities are yet to be finalised Also Read: Hindustan Zinc plans Rs 50k-crore capex pipeline for next 5 years The remaining expansion, which will take capacity to 650 KT, will require investment in a similar proportion over the next four to five years \"That translates to an average annual capex of about Rs 7,000-8,000 crore,\" Misra said, adding that only 15-20% of this multi-year investment plan will translate into actual cash outflows during the current financial year.",
